                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of worshipper. Cf. kidnapper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b9959b1e-db04-4b64-a413-6558a8f0c749",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8b5bd03-b6c8-3221-854f-59135418d49f",
                        "target_lang_word": "adorer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "adorer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "317c0b3a-88ca-3ce9-a0b2-d51116e09b9f",
                                        "entry_id": "5751aa61-8f07-3129-8b39-9fa6f528b2d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who adores.",
                                            "Someone who worships."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fef78134-be2e-4fdf-bba7-b03bb829b77c",
                                                "sense_id": "317c0b3a-88ca-3ce9-a0b2-d51116e09b9f",
                                                "text": "1582, Gregory Martin (translator), The New Testament of Jesus Christ, Translated Faithfully into English, Reims: John Fogny, John 4.23, p. 226,\nBut the houre commeth, and now it is, when the true adorers shal adore the Father in spirit and veritie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "432e7344-67e5-46da-aead-a6cc45cdf17a",
                                                "sense_id": "317c0b3a-88ca-3ce9-a0b2-d51116e09b9f",
                                                "text": "[…] I in one Night freed / From servitude inglorious welnigh half / Th’ Angelic Name, and thinner left the throng / Of his adorers […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3fbab3a-32c6-4e0b-a1ed-3918c002d553",
                                                "sense_id": "317c0b3a-88ca-3ce9-a0b2-d51116e09b9f",
                                                "text": "All men in the outset of the religion they profess are adorers of a God, and friends of man."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "269549fc-e6da-345f-ba9e-6ae6ecb7a348",
                                        "entry_id": "5751aa61-8f07-3129-8b39-9fa6f528b2d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who adores.",
                                            "Someone who has a deep admiration, fondness or love (of someone or something)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3c0319d-7b31-4adc-894a-e7d8e81a6ccf",
                                                "sense_id": "269549fc-e6da-345f-ba9e-6ae6ecb7a348",
                                                "text": "[…] I profess myself her adorer, not her friend."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05bae697-295e-446d-92bd-f27d69e2a30a",
                                                "sense_id": "269549fc-e6da-345f-ba9e-6ae6ecb7a348",
                                                "text": "I vvho profeſs my ſelf an Admirer, an Adorer of Reaſon, am obliged to ovvn, that in ſome Caſes the Sharpneſs of Ridicule can do more than the Strength of Argument."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75ee864a-46fe-4722-94f2-716bcf957242",
                                                "sense_id": "269549fc-e6da-345f-ba9e-6ae6ecb7a348",
                                                "text": "When rival adorers come courting a maid, / There’s something or other may often be said, / Why he should be pitched upon rather than him. / This wasn’t the case with Old Paul and Old Tim."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a135d703-e54f-47a4-8d40-56d44325e832",
                                                "sense_id": "269549fc-e6da-345f-ba9e-6ae6ecb7a348",
                                                "text": "The funny thing was that all the envelopes were addressed in the same hand, in green or sometimes purple capitals. It was like one crazed adorer laying siege to Leo."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a2758c6d-2819-42c0-8bee-6b67388b7f59",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8b5bd03-b6c8-3221-854f-59135418d49f",
                        "target_lang_word": "votaress",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "votaress",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5605b896-64fd-3bc7-a261-9ed53e0338f0",
                                        "entry_id": "11bfec51-c342-351a-82fb-469e3611ec95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female votary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d26db18-edf4-4448-9524-e1c9fb27657a",
                                                "sense_id": "5605b896-64fd-3bc7-a261-9ed53e0338f0",
                                                "text": "a votaress of the order"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "003088b5-a994-4ed0-89bc-ad578f4393c6",
                                                "sense_id": "5605b896-64fd-3bc7-a261-9ed53e0338f0",
                                                "text": "His seeming rescue by a votaress of the high priestess of the sun had been but a part of the mimicry of their heathen ceremony—the sun looking down upon him through the opening at the top of the court had claimed him as his own, and the priestess had come from the inner temple to save him from the polluting hands of worldlings—to save him as a human offering to their flaming deity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "489410ce-f8e6-44cf-b35b-816414bddffe",
                                                "sense_id": "5605b896-64fd-3bc7-a261-9ed53e0338f0",
                                                "text": "Madness grew in the eyes of the capering votaress and was reflected in the eyes of the watchers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "941b292e-bd0f-4217-b58f-6396b8804ac3",
                                                "sense_id": "5605b896-64fd-3bc7-a261-9ed53e0338f0",
                                                "text": "Aminta, of course, falls in love with Sylvia at first sight, and she, chaste votaress of Diana, is outraged."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
